48
00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:45.250
Choose one AI product behavior you have
seen. Identify what

49
00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:50.500
came from the model, supplied context,
retrieval or search, memory,

50
00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:55.750
a tool, deterministic code, or an agentic
loop. Mark anything

51
00:04:55.750 --> 00:05:01.000
you cannot verify as unknown.

52
00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:37.429
Fluent language, confident tone, detailed
structure, and citation-shaped text are

53
00:06:37.429 --> 00:06:43.857
not evidence. A model can fabricate a
source, merge separate

54
00:06:43.857 --> 00:06:50.286
facts, use stale knowledge, omit a
limitation, inherit bias, misunderstand

55
00:06:50.286 --> 00:06:56.714
context, produce incompatible numbers, or
vary across runs. It does

56
00:06:56.714 --> 00:07:03.143
not automatically know private systems,
today's events, local policy, or

57
00:07:03.143 --> 00:07:09.571
the user's unstated goal. Context is
finite and may contain

58
00:07:09.571 --> 00:07:16.000
conflicts or malicious instructions.
Retrieval can return the wrong page.

59
00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:22.429
Tools can fail or report uncertain
outcomes. Code can compile

60
00:07:22.429 --> 00:07:28.857
incorrectly or look correct without
running. A generated explanation of

61
00:07:28.857 --> 00:07:35.286
success is not the same as a verified
postcondition. Treat

62
00:07:35.286 --> 00:07:41.714
output as a candidate. Ask which claims
matter, what evidence

63
00:07:41.714 --> 00:07:48.143
would support them, whether the evidence
matches version and scope,

64
00:07:48.143 --> 00:07:54.571
and what remains unknown. Uncertainty that
is visible can be

65
00:07:54.571 --> 00:08:01.000
managed; unsupported confidence cannot.

66
00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:08.000
Checkpoint. A model confidently states the
current employee leave policy

67
00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:15.000
and provides no source. The answer sounds
professional and matches

68
00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:22.000
what a manager remembers from last year.
Can the employee

69
00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:29.000
rely on it, and what evidence is required?

70
00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:33.000
Do not rely on the answer. Professional
wording and a

71
00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:37.000
manager's memory do not establish the
current policy. Open the

72
00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:41.000
authoritative policy source, confirm its
effective date, covered employee group,

73
00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:45.000
location, exceptions, and approval owner.
If the current source is

74
00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:49.000
unavailable or ambiguous, report the gap
and contact the responsible

75
00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:53.000
human function. If you accepted the answer
because two uncertain

76
00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:57.000
signals agreed, revise the rule: generated
confidence plus memory is

77
00:09:57.000 --> 00:10:01.000
not independent current evidence. If you
rejected all AI assistance,

78
00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:05.000
narrow that conclusion. AI may help
explain the verified policy,

79
00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:09.000
but it cannot replace the source or
accountable decision.

80
00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:14.714
Choose tasks by consequence and
inspectability. Brainstorming, first

81
00:10:14.714 --> 00:10:20.429
drafts, restructuring permitted text,
